& [Purpose] is observation without reconciliation
  + run an exact validator-profile schema reader and actual typed serde reader over one root-qualified subject
  + preserve each branch result even when its peer differs
  + expose representation and rule evidence without adopting engine messages as identity
  + leave case expectation agreement semantic validity and authority to later explicit stages

& [PrerequisiteOrder] is I03A then I03B then I03C then I03D
  + I03A must activate exact dependency lock and explicit no-resolution construction
  + I03B must release one faithful immutable input before input readers run
  + I03C must compile stable residual identity before residual carry
  + documentary formation does not satisfy or bypass any prerequisite

& [RootBindings] are exact
  + prepare_input input_deserialize PrepareRequest
  + run_input input_deserialize PreparedRunRequest
  + verify_input input_deserialize VerifyRequest
  + base_response output_serialize ProcedureToolResponse with base-response fixture assertion
  + preparation_response output_serialize ProcedureToolResponse with preparation-response fixture assertion
  + root kind direction type document intended use and dependency profile form one binding digest

& [ResponseRootDelineation] is explicit
  + base document is 53014 bytes SHA256 40FD8536021892ADB35CECBCA717AD2CA68FA5125A3C027FC8274364FCE1B77C
  + preparation document is 53021 bytes SHA256 9D51B85036B9A4FF7C519693F60C6ECF99C7CC5E529EF7DB423365D776C7B51A
  + their schema values are equal after removal of dollar id
  + equal validation behavior cannot merge document digest root identity or intended-use obligations

& [InputPipeline] is fixed
  * verify root binding document registry validator receipt faithful instance and digest agreement
  * branch exact retained bytes to schema Value projection and actual typed deserializer independently
  * require explicit typed deserializer end
  * validate the Value only after representation succeeds
  * normalize each complete branch without comparing it
  * construct ReaderPair only after all shared identities agree

& [OutputPipeline] is fixed
  * verify root binding document registry validator receipt and typed fixture envelope
  * serialize the actual ProcedureToolResponse twice and require exact byte equality
  * run I03B over the first serialized bytes
  * materialize Value and validate the root document
  * emit typed serialization and schema observations independently
  * preserve intended-use assertion as evidence without semantically proving it

& [Independence] is strict
  + schema branch receives no typed value
  + typed input branch receives original bytes and never schema Value
  + neither branch repairs filters interprets or overrides peer output
  + a completed branch survives peer rejection or exhaustion

& [ReaderDisposition] is accepted rejected exhausted internal_fault not_applicable or skipped_dependency
& [ObservationStage] is binding representation validation deserialization serialization completion or normalization
  + accepted and rejected mean the declared reader completed
  + exhausted means a finite representation finding or recursion capacity prevented completion
  + skipped_dependency blocks proof rather than acting as not_applicable
  + internal_fault blocks proof and cannot be compared as a reader decision

& [DependencyProfile] binds exact activated jsonschema serde serde_json checksums features source and Cargo lock digests
  + formation observes serde 1.0.229 and serde_json 1.0.151 in the current lock
  + jsonschema remains absent from the current lock
  + I03D activation rebinds the post-I03A exact lock rather than copying formation observations

& [ValidatorConfiguration] is explicit
  + jsonschema exact candidate 0.49.2 default-features false
  + Draft 2020-12 selected explicitly
  + should_validate_formats false
  + should_ignore_unknown_formats true
  + no custom format keyword registry or resource callback
  + exact schema id dialect document digest closure and local-reference preflight before build

& [NoResolution] is defense in depth
  + compile graph excludes resolve-http resolve-file resolve-async and TLS transport features
  + a structural preflight permits only resolvable in-document fragment references
  + Cantor installs an owned zero-sized deny retriever because the library always owns a retriever interface
  + every retrieve call deterministically returns denial without file network environment registry cache or fallback access
  + any invocation is internal_fault because preflight should have made it unreachable

& [MetaAndConstruction] are honestly related
  + explicit draft202012 meta validation produces a MetaSchemaObservation
  + validator construction follows only an accepted meta result
  + public jsonschema build repeats its internal schema check and that repeated gate cannot be disabled through public API
  + construction disposition is reported separately but not represented as operationally independent meta execution

& [ReferencePreflight] is structured
  + recursively inspect schema-bearing object and array positions under finite document limits
  + permit dollar schema only as the exact root Draft 2020-12 dialect declaration
  + classify dollar id as identity and never retrieval permission
  + permit dollar ref only when target is a valid fragment whose JSON Pointer or anchor resolves in the same document
  + refuse external relative empty-base HTTP HTTPS file UNC drive data opaque dynamic missing malformed escaping and over-limit targets before build
  + record keyword location raw target digest resolved location disposition and exact counts

& [FormatSemantics] are annotations
  + exact artifact values are int64 uint32 and uint64
  + no format finding exists under this profile
  + actual Rust typed binding supplies destination range enforcement
  + schema acceptance with typed range rejection is preserved disagreement evidence and not validator failure

& [SchemaRepresentation] is selected-engine evidence
  + exact source digest remains authoritative for bytes
  + bounded serde_json Value is a separate projection with canonical digest
  + every I03B numeric token receives exact_i64 exact_u64 finite_f64 or representation_exhausted class
  + finite_f64 is explicitly approximate relative to mathematical decimal meaning
  + integer beyond u64 or unrepresentable number exhausts at representation stage before validation
  + Value syntax or EOF failure after I03B pass is internal_fault

& [KeywordInventory] is exact for the I02 baseline
  + schema structure uses dollar defs dollar id dollar ref dollar schema items patternProperties properties required title and format
  + stable rejection classes are additional_properties any_of constant enum maximum minimum maximum_length minimum_length one_of pattern required type and unique_items
  + pattern backtrack limit is exhausted
  + regex engine failure reference failure after preflight and unseen error kind are internal_fault
  + unseen kind is labeled profile_drift and never dynamically expands the stable enum

& [SchemaFinding] contains root binding document source and projection digests rule class instance schema and evaluation paths optional absolute keyword location owned rule context context digest advisory and finding digest
  + context carries only exact bounded rule parameters or their canonical digest
  + finding identity excludes Display Debug iterator order and prose
  + findings sort by instance path schema path evaluation path rule class context digest and finding id

& [FindingCapacity] is atomic
  + accepted requires zero findings
  + rejected requires one through 256 findings and attempted count equal retained count
  + a 257th finding changes disposition to exhausted at normalization
  + exhausted observation carries attempted count of at least 257 and no authoritative finding prefix

& [TypedInput] is actual
  + serde_json Deserializer reads exact original bytes
  + root binding chooses only PrepareRequest PreparedRunRequest or VerifyRequest
  + successful value construction is followed by end
  + success creates deterministic serialized TypedProjection digest
  + projection is normalized evidence and never claimed to reproduce source ordering escapes whitespace or number spelling

& [TypedOutput] is actual
  + OutputFixtureEnvelope contains exact root fixture id fixture digest intended-use assertion proof reference and actual ProcedureToolResponse
  + serialize twice with serde_json and require byte identity
  + output bytes and digest become I03B and schema observation subject
  + serializer success does not prove fixture intended use or business semantics

& [SerdeFault] uses category io syntax data or eof plus exact activated-version line and column
  + data is typed rejection
  + syntax or EOF after I03B input acceptance is cross-reader internal_fault
  + I/O from slice input is internal_fault
  + bounded advisory text is excluded from identity
  + line and column are reader locators and not JSON paths or byte offsets

& [Observations] are closed
  + SchemaObservation binds validator receipt source Value projection numeric projections disposition stage findings accounts and digest
  + SerdeObservation binds source or fixture typed projection disposition stage optional fault repeat digest accounts and digest
  + no durable observation retains the ephemeral typed value or sensitive field contents

& [ReaderPair] binds profile root binding subject document registry applicable residual ids both observations and pair digest
  + residual ids resolve through I03C and retain registry disposition
  - never: agreement pass conformant compatible semantic valid admitted executable or authoritative field

& [PairFaults] are stale_binding stale_document stale_registry subject_mismatch wrong_direction wrong_type wrong_intended_use prerequisite_inactive limit_exceeded or internal_fault
  + one atomic fault replaces the entire pair
  + shared identity failure cannot yield partial observations

& [Resources] are exact
  + maximum projection bytes 16777216 for each reader
  + maximum findings 256
  + maximum diagnostic characters 1024
  + maximum path segments 128 and path characters 4096
  + maximum local references 4096 target bytes 4096 and pointer segments 128
  + I03B input structural limits remain authoritative
  + every count span and byte accumulation uses checked arithmetic

& [FutureSourceTouch] is unsigned and exact
  + modify crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/lib.rs under separately activated schema-conformance feature
  + add crates/cantor_procedure_tool/src/reader_observation.rs including CantorDenyRetriever
  + add crates/cantor_procedure_tool/tests/reader_observation.rs
  - never: I03D Cargo lock dependency core enforcement schema golden CLI MCP service ecosystem preflight provider model effect or hardware file

& [Proof] after future activation is adversarial
  + five root bindings and exact response-root distinction
  + meta preflight construction representation schema and typed accepted rejected exhausted and internal cases
  + thirteen schema rule classes exact context paths digests and sort order
  + serde data syntax EOF and impossible I/O categories
  + exact_i64 exact_u64 finite_f64 beyond-u64 fractional exponent and destination range disagreement witnesses
  + local external missing malformed escaping and deny-retriever references
  + finding 255 256 and 257 projection path reference and recursion boundaries
  + repeat typed output and complete ReaderPair digest equality
  + proof of zero semantic admission provider model service persistence network effect or hardware invocation

& [FormationBoundary] is strict
  + current slice adds source SJS canonical exploded requirements justification plan review inactive lock proof narrative and evidence metadata only
  - never: dependency Cargo Rust parser validator reader corpus comparison semantic compatibility admission provider model service persistence network effect production hardware or FPGA

& [PresentDisposition] is formed_not_activated
